Sval: native messaging, managed storage and PKCS#11 manifests are Sval's own

Firefox and Sval run side by side without touching each other's state.
Gecko reads extension host, managed storage and PKCS#11 manifests from
folders every Firefox-family app shares: ~/Library/Application
Support/Mozilla and /Library/Application Support/Mozilla on macOS,
~/.mozilla and /usr/lib/mozilla on Linux, and Software\Mozilla in the
Windows registry. Sval reads them from its own: the user's application
data directory (~/Library/Application Support/Sval, ~/.sval), the system
twin (/Library/Application Support/Sval, the system configuration
directory /etc/sval), and Software\Sval.

The Certificates policy looks for a bare file name in the same folders on
macOS and Linux, and on Windows in the Mozilla directories in AppData,
which it reached through the user extension directory that Sval turns
off. On Windows it looks in the application data directory.

Mozilla's native messaging tests write the registry key NativeManifests
reads.

